When Each Approach Is Appropriate
Approach	Appropriate situation
Byte-by-byte reading	Small files or simple demonstrations
BufferedInputStream	Large files, sequential processing and limited memory
Files.readAllLines()	Small or moderate files when all lines are needed simultaneously

Final Comparison and Decision
For the 50 MB attendance log, I would choose BufferedInputStream because it provides efficient sequential reading while using only a small, fixed amount of additional memory.

Files.readAllLines() is easier to implement and is useful when the application needs to access all lines repeatedly. However, it can consume excessive memory when processing large attendance logs.

Final decision: Buffered reading is the most suitable solution for this problem because it reduces underlying file-read operations, maintains O(S) processing time and requires only O(B) additional memory.
